\"off\"></label></div><button id=\"example\" type=\"button\">Fictional example</button><button id=\"reset\" type=\"button\">Clear</button></fieldset><div class=\"results\" aria-live=\"polite\"><div><strong>Calculated refund</strong><output id=\"expected\">—</output></div><div><strong>Calculated refund minus amount received</strong><output id=\"delta\">—</output></div></div><p id=\"status\" role=\"status\">Enter all three amounts. A blank is unknown, not zero.</p><h2>Before returning the property</h2><details><summary>Move-out dates and procedure</summary><p>Check notice dates and procedure in your own agreement; do not rely on a universal notice period.</p></details><details><summary>Condition and inventory</summary><p>Compare the property with your move-in notes and record discrepancies.</p></details><details><summary>Meters and payments</summary><p>Compare meter readings, bills and amounts already paid.</p></details><details><summary>Inspection and keys</summary><p>Clarify inspection, key return and evidence of handover.</p></details><details><summary>Deposit refund</summary><p>Ask for an understandable breakdown of deductions and compare actual receipts with the records.</p></details><small>Local draft. Do not enter addresses, names, contacts or payment details. The tool does not send or store values. Your browser may restore fields. Not legal advice, a payment demand or refund confirmation.</small></main><div id=\"copy\" hidden>{\"title\": \"Move-out and deposit reconciliation\", \"intro\": \"Compare your entered refund calculation with the amount actually received. This is arithmetic, not a legal determination of debt. Entered deductions are not deemed agreed or lawful.\", \"fields\": [\"Deposit paid\", \"Deductions in the available calculation\", \"Refund actually received\"], \"expected\": \"Calculated refund\", \"delta\": \"Calculated refund minus amount received\", \"unknown\": \"Enter all three amounts. A blank is unknown, not zero.\", \"invalid\": \"Enter